      "level": 2,
      "content": "The Himalayas"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "The Northern Plains are formed by alluvial deposition from the Indus, Ganga, and Brahmaputra river systems.",
        "The Northern Plains are extremely fertile and serve as India's agricultural core, producing ~50% of its wheat and >90% of its rice.",
        "Flooding in the plains is driven by heavy monsoon rainfall, sediment-choked riverbeds, poor management, and deforestation.",
        "Expansion of the Thar Desert is driven by mining, deforestation, climate changes, groundwater overuse, and dune spread."
      ],
      "id": "v64mlzb"
    },
